# The Dockerfile copies only `requirements*.txt` and `app/`, but the build context is uploaded
# to the remote builder in full before any COPY runs. Without this file that upload includes
# `data/` — 8 GB of GLBs and SQLite databases the image never uses, since the public instance
# reads its assets from R2 and its rows from Postgres.
#
# Everything the running app needs lives under `app/` (templates, static, app/data) and is NOT
# excluded here.

data/
public_bundle/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.venv/
venv/

tests/
docs/
scripts/
notebooks/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/

# The research stack is deliberately not installed in the image (deploy/README.md); keeping the
# file out of the context makes that hard to undo by accident.
requirements-research.txt
requirements-dev.txt
